---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Receipt from '../components/Receipt.astro';

/**
 * Home. Governed by CLAIMS.md — every technical sentence on this page traces to
 * an EVIDENCE.md entry in the mngd repo, and the entry is named next to the
 * claim rather than kept in a drawer:
 *
 *   the repository inside the product, clone-out, fast-forward law  E-116
 *   the three gates, each seen to fail alone                        E-112
 *   a refusal whose recovery advice can actually succeed            E-125
 *   applying compiles desired state from the hosted repository      E-119
 *   the Air installed Chrome and named the declaration              E-130
 *
 * No superlatives, no counts, no logos, no testimonials, and nothing about a
 * capability that is not running. The ceiling on the whole page is the sentence
 * in the "observation" note below, and it is deliberately the weakest form of
 * the claim that is still true.
 */

const loop = [
  {
    step: '01',
    title: 'Propose',
    body:
      'A change to the fleet is a branch in the repository, with its title, author and date read off the tip commit. Nothing about the proposal lives in a table that could disagree with git.',
    cite: 'E-116',
  },
  {
    step: '02',
    title: 'Read the refusal',
    body:
      'Three gates run in-process and answer in plain English, each able to fail on its own. A refusal names what is wrong and what to run next — and the command it recommends has to be able to succeed against the state that produced it.',
    cite: 'E-112 · E-125',
  },
  {
    step: '03',
    title: 'Apply the commit you were shown',
    body:
      'Fast-forward only, as a law rather than a limitation: the merged tree IS the reviewed tree. Applying compiles desired state out of the repository this instance hosts, not out of something baked into a release.',
    cite: 'E-119',
  },
  {
    step: '04',
    title: 'Let the Mac answer',
    body:
      'Desired state and device-reported state sit side by side. When the console says an app is installed, that is the device attesting it — including the identifier of the declaration it says caused the install.',
    cite: 'E-130',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="mngd — the fleet repository lives inside the product"
  description="Apple device management where the fleet repository lives inside the product: propose a change, read the gates' refusal in plain English, apply the commit you were shown, and let the Mac say what it did."
>
  <!-- ── Hero ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-wide) px-(--gutter) pt-16 pb-14 max-sm:px-5 sm:pt-24">
    <div class="max-w-[54rem]">
      <div class="eyebrow mb-6">Machinery Software · Apple device management</div>

      <h1 class="text-[clamp(34px,6vw,60px)] text-ink">
        The fleet repository lives<br class="max-sm:hidden" />
        <span class="text-muted">inside the product.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[56ch] text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted sm:text-[18px]">
        mngd hosts your fleet repository itself. Propose a change, read the gates'
        refusal in plain English, apply the exact commit you were shown — then read
        what the Mac says it did, in its own words.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a
          href="/early-access"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-accent px-5 py-2.5 text-[15px] font-medium text-accent-contrast no-underline transition-colors hover:bg-accent-strong"
        >
          Join the waitlist
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 11L11 3M6 3h5v5" /></svg>
        </a>
        <a
          href="#receipt"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-2.5 text-[15px] font-medium text-ink no-underline transition-colors hover:bg-hover"
        >
          Read the receipt
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-5 max-w-[56ch] text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-faint">
        mngd is early and not generally available. There is no trial to start and no
        account to create yet — the waitlist is the whole front door, and what is
        below is what has actually run.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── The loop ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-wide) px-(--gutter) py-14 max-sm:px-5">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-6">The loop</div>
    <h2 class="max-w-[30ch] text-[clamp(24px,3.4vw,34px)] text-ink">
      Propose, refuse, apply, attest.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[60ch] text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      In the mode mngd hosts the repository, the whole loop runs on a directory: no
      forge, no external CI service, no credential, no token, and nothing to
      configure on somebody else's server.
      <span class="text-faint">[E-116]</span>
    </p>

    <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-line sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {loop.map(s => (
        <li class="flex flex-col bg-surface p-6">
          <div class="font-mono text-[11px] text-faint">{s.step}</div>
          <h3 class="mt-4 text-[15.5px] text-ink">{s.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2.5 flex-1 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted">{s.body}</p>
          <div class="receipt-cite mt-4">{s.cite}</div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- ── The receipt ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section id="receipt" class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-wide) px-(--gutter) py-14 max-sm:px-5">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-6">A receipt, quoted</div>
    <h2 class="max-w-[34ch] text-[clamp(24px,3.4vw,34px)] text-ink">
      When the console says installed, that is the Mac talking.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[62ch] text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      On 2026-09-11 a MacBook Air installed Google Chrome from a declaration this
      repository holds, and reported back with the version on the device and the
      identifier of the declaration it says caused it. Both panels below are quoted
      out of the device page — the left is what git asked for, the right is what the
      Mac answered.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <Receipt label="Declared — what git asks for" text={`Google Chrome 153.0.8010.37
com.google.Chrome
from roles/baseline/com.mngd.package.google-chrome.json
role baseline
declaration com.mngd.package.google-chrome

Install behaviour          Required`} />
      <Receipt label="Reported — what the Mac says" text={`installed
version on the device: 153.0.8010.37
name: Google Chrome

Because git said so       the device names this declaration
                          com.mngd.package.google-chrome

Verdict                   installed`} />
    </div>

    <p class="receipt-cite mt-1">
      E-130 — one MacBook Air against a staging instance, panel timestamped
      2026-09-11 12:30 UTC. No agent was involved: macOS did the install because a
      declaration told it to.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ── What is proven, and where ──────────────────────────────────────
       The honest section. A marketing page that quotes a receipt owes the
       reader the boundary of that receipt in the same breath, or the receipt is
       doing a job it did not earn. -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-wide) px-(--gutter) py-14 max-sm:px-5">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-6">What is proven, and where</div>
    <h2 class="max-w-[34ch] text-[clamp(24px,3.4vw,34px)] text-ink">
      Two different words: on hardware, and in a container.
    </h2>

    <dl class="mt-8 divide-y divide-rowline overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface">
      <div class="grid gap-1 p-5 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-[15px] text-ink">A Mac installed a package because a declaration said so</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
            One MacBook Air, watched on the device page, reported by the device. [E-130]
          </dd>
        </div>
        <dd class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-wide text-ok-ink">on hardware</dd>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-1 p-5 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-[15px] text-ink">Propose, gate, apply, and compile from the hosted repository</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
            Run end to end in its own container with a generated admin token. No device
            was involved in this one. [E-112, E-116, E-119]
          </dd>
        </div>
        <dd class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-wide text-warn-ink">in a container</dd>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-1 p-5 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-[15px] text-ink">Everything else</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
            Not claimed here. When a thing has been watched working, it gets a Field Note
            and an evidence ID; until then this page stays quiet about it.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <dd class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-wide text-faint">not yet</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <!-- The ceiling CLAIMS.md sets on this whole page, stated as the observation
         it is. Not "the first", not "the only". -->
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-[62ch] border-l-2 border-faint-line pl-4 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-faint italic">
      We haven't seen another MDM that hosts the repository itself. That is an
      observation about what we have looked at, not a claim about what exists —
      config-as-code for Apple fleets is a road with other people already on it, and
      <a href="/credits" class="text-accent not-italic no-underline hover:underline">they are named here</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Bottom CTA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-wide) px-(--gutter) pt-8 pb-4 max-sm:px-5">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-8 sm:p-12">
      <h2 class="max-w-[26ch] text-[clamp(22px,3vw,30px)] text-ink">
        Want to watch this get built?
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-[56ch] text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The waitlist gets the Field Notes — what ran, what refused, and what the
        device said, with the evidence ID attached. No launch dates, because there
        aren't any.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a
          href="/early-access"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-accent px-5 py-2.5 text-[15px] font-medium text-accent-contrast no-underline transition-colors hover:bg-accent-strong"
        >
          Join the waitlist
        </a>
        <a
          href="/blog"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-line px-5 py-2.5 text-[15px] font-medium text-ink no-underline transition-colors hover:bg-hover"
        >
          Read the Field Notes
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
